From 9dc29cb2d64f871c079ba710362506c46a2d33fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:17:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(worker): flush allocator and host heap across startup
 preparation and capture phases

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 4652b632a3c6bf5f65da7d2bfb750b203e671aa2.

Rationale:
On 119 GiB unified-memory GB10 nodes at TP=3, startup memory dips during CUDA graph capture and tail-shape warmup when unreferenced blocks in the default expandable-segments caching allocator remain reserved alongside global_graph_pool allocations:
1. GPUModelRunner.capture_model() previously ran target graph capture, DFlash query graph capture, DSpark context graph capture, and AdaptiveVerificationManager.warm_tail_shapes() back-to-back inside freeze_gc_for_cudagraph_capture() with a single empty_cache() at the end.
2. AdaptiveVerificationManager.warm_tail_shapes() ran eager dummy passes across ascending tail token counts (384, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 6155) without synchronizing and flushing the caching allocator between passes, leaving ~1.88 GiB of uncoalesced intermediate segments reserved during the 6,155-token pass before the final empty_cache().
3. DFlashSpeculator.capture() and DSparkContextCudaGraphs.capture() ran eager capacity warmups before graph capture without flushing the default allocator before entering CudaGraphManager.capture(), and prepare.release_host_memory() called malloc_trim(0) without gc.collect() or empty_cache().

Flush the default caching allocator between target and speculator capture, between DFlash query and DSpark context capture, after DSpark context capacity warmups, after each eager pass in warm_tail_shapes() (moved outside freeze_gc_for_cudagraph_capture()), and inside prepare.release_host_memory().

Quality:
Bit- and instruction-identical at runtime: only reclaims unreferenced host heap and default-allocator segments during startup before readiness; zero change to weights, kernels, captured CUDA graphs, KV cache sizes, or serving steps.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py tests/v1/worker/test_prepare_kernels.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_dspark_context.py (113 passed).

Upstream status: local startup memory optimization for unified-memory GB10 nodes.
